          {
            "commit": "3f4a0cf4a81995b5f15a1f3ed078b111282bbc2c",
            "subject": "LU-20720 osd-ldiskfs: read the inode table, not the inodes"
          }
        ],
        "author": {
          "name": "Hiroshi Nishida",
          "email": "hnishida@thelustrecollective.com",
          "date": "2026-09-10 22:11:36.000000000",
          "tz": -420
        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "Hiroshi Nishida",
          "email": "hnishida@thelustrecollective.com",
          "date": "2026-09-10 22:11:36.000000000",
          "tz": -420
        },
        "subject": "LU-20720 osd: xattrs from the otable iterator",
        "message": "LU-20720 osd: xattrs from the otable iterator\n\nAn object's FID and attributes do not say whether it has a layout,\nwhat its SOM size is, or what it is named; its xattrs do.\n\nDORA_XATTR asks the iterator for a named xattr while it still holds\nthe object.  On ldiskfs an inline xattr is in the inode-table block\nthe iterator has, so the common case costs no read; an external\nblock is read when it must be.  On ZFS the bonus buffer answers the\nsame way.  osd_otable_it_xattr() is the per-backend entry point.\n\nDORA_STATS reserves counters for how those reads divide between the\ntiers, since whether the common case really is free is the number\nthis rests on.\n\nSigned-off-by: Hiroshi Nishida <hnishida@thelustrecollective.com>\nTest-Parameters: ignore\nChange-Id: I56d22811982edcaae48ed78366a230388960f6d2\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
